cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Breaking the Extraction Bottleneck: A Single AI Agent Achieves Equivalence with Published Meta-Analysis Data Across Three Agricultural Datasets"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Halpern"
    given-names: "Moshe"
    affiliation: "Institute of Soil, Water and Environmental Sciences, Agricultural Research Organization – Volcani Center, Israel"
repository-code: "https://github.com/halpernmoshe/Meta-analysis-extractor-agriculture"
url: "https://github.com/halpernmoshe/Meta-analysis-extractor-agriculture"
abstract: >-
  A single AI agent (Claude Opus 4.6) extracts quantitative data from
  scientific PDFs for meta-analysis, validated against three published
  plant science datasets (1,184 observations, 87 papers) with formal
  ICC, CCC, TOST equivalence testing, and Bland-Altman analysis.
  Also includes an independent multi-model consensus pipeline for
  ground-truth-free cross-method validation.
keywords:
  - meta-analysis
  - data extraction
  - large language models
  - AI agent
  - automation
  - plant science
  - systematic review
  - equivalence testing
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-03-16"
